# board-phone's FAQ edits, re-applied on the newest live faq.md just before zipping (CLAUDE.md)
import sys
p=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p).read()
old1="(on a phone, a row along the top). **Board** opens first, with **Is it delivering?**; **Development** is its own page from the left. Across the top, **What's wrong now**: a chip each for Trips, Warnings, Caps, Checks, Sync (Railway and the sync, when their watch needs a look) and Paused now, with its count. A chip opens its short list; each item opens its part in the side panel."
new1="(on a phone, under **☰** at the top left, which names the page you're on). **Board** opens first, with **Is it delivering?**; **Development** is its own page from the left. At the top, **Alerts**, with the board's one alarm count (2026-11-24): every open trip and every warning not yet seen, the same number as the light in the top bar, the Board count and the alarm list's **Open**; beside it, each group's count, as \"2 trips · 9 warnings · 2 caps\". It opens to its groups, each with its count: Trips, Waiting for its run (trips started again, amber, until that run works), Warnings, Caps, Checks, Sync (Railway and the sync, when their watch needs a look), Seen (warnings someone has seen, listed but not counted: the system is still handling them) and Paused now (what's paused, counted on its own, never added to the alarms). A part whose trips were all started again reads **Waiting for its run** (amber), on its cards and its row, until that run works. Each item opens its part in the side panel. Notices aren't alarms to act on: they're in the alarm list under **Notices**. The alarm table under **Diagnostics → Alarms** says the same number for **Open**, and the queue's filter shows with the queue, under **Diagnostics → Observation and reporting**."
assert s.count(old1)==1, 'faq 1'; s=s.replace(old1,new1)
old2="- **The light in the admin's top bar:** on every module page, the count of open trips and warnings; it opens the alarm list."
new2="- **The light in the admin's top bar:** on every module page, the count of open trips (seen or not, pressed and waiting for their run or not) and of warnings not yet seen, the same number as the board's **Alerts**; red only for a trip still holding, amber for warnings and for trips started again and waiting for their run; it opens the alarm list."
assert s.count(old2)==1, 'faq 2'; s=s.replace(old2,new2)
open(p,'w').write(s)
